## SEVERITY / VERDICT
*Blocker:* a path beyond the three; numstat not `164 0` / `23 11` / `3 3`; the test file not blob `f9817d98`; a validators diff not set-equal to `9a61d39e`; commit 1 NOT red on the strip and reject cells, a control red at commit 1, or commit 2 not 39/39 green; a DEFECT found by a mutant or a probe; an (A) bypass inside the aim that reaches a sink; a catastrophic (exponential) regex shape; a NEW CodeQL alert with security severity high+ or rule severity `error`, an open instance of #83, #84 or #43 on the PR ref, **#136 open on the PR ref (the C-209 amendment's blocking case: Blocker candidate, graded in the verdict line with reasoning)**, or a `CodeQL` check-run concluded failure; a counts delta other than +39 tests +1 suite; a conflict at merge or a merge-result tree different from main plus the three files; a gitleaks finding; a person name, decision-card id or secret in an added line, message or the PR text; the head moved. *Major:* a mutant TEST GAP on a ruled-in input; a bypass classified (A) outside the aim with a rule-backed reason; a shape over 1 s at the body limit on an unauthenticated route; a real route value altered by the strip (3d); a builder claim contradicted by your measurement that changes the verdict's basis (a blob sha, a red/green count, a verify figure, the flipped set); `Build` red at the head for a reason not shown to be a base fact; a repo rule against non-ASCII found for the test file. *Minor/Note:* a TEST GAP beyond the aim; a quadratic-but-fast shape (with the figure); (B) and (C) classified candidates; the 13 non-ASCII bytes in the byte-equal test file (a Note unless a rule is found); the commits unsigned; a ticket key in a message; node version differing from CI; the `mergeable_state` text; the stale-main Known fact (B4); load-rule remarks.
**VERDICT RULES.** GO needs every check-run at the head completed and green (the neutral `CodeQL` summary replaced by a completed conclusion), all three Analyze runs complete with both thresholds met and #136 not open on the PR ref, `Build` completed green (the B4 rule applies), Checks 1-4, 6, 7 clean and measured, and the mutant matrix and the bypass hunt printed in full. While `build` or any Analyze run is pending the verdict is at most GO WITH FINDINGS and the line above the last line names the pending set. A NO GO sends a fix to a new builder seat: state the fix-shape in prose and a ONE-line question for the product owner only if a ruling is needed (a finding that asks for a redesign, such as escape-on-output, is a ruling for the product owner, never a defect of this PR); round 1 of 2 under the cap, a second NO GO on the same class goes to the product owner. **Escalation: none upward (you are tier 1). STOP (`STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY <the change and why>`) if** the delta holds a path beyond the three, a change to `.github/**`, `backend/server.js` or the harness, a secret, a request that leaves loopback (other than GitHub GETs, the one Jira GET if you need it, the npm registry as `npm ci` itself reaches it), or a security-shaped finding you cannot classify by the list above (your own scratch plants are scratch, not a delta).
**First line of STATUS (the verdict line; at Step 0 the placeholder `GATE VERDICT B647: PENDING`):** `GATE VERDICT B647: pr112 <GO|GO WITH FINDINGS|NO GO> @ 412c784 (round 1 of 2 - delta <3 commits, 3 paths, +190 -14, numstat 164/0 23/11 3/3 y/n; cells blob f9817d98 y/n; validators diff set-equal to 9a61d39e y/n; other paths byte-equal y/n> - red-first <commit 1: r failed / g passed of 39, controls green y/n; commit 2: 39/39 y/n; flipped n> - mutants <k of m killed as predicted; survivors: equivalent n / test gap n / defect n> - bypass hunt <candidates n; A n / B n / C n; cross-stage assembly <found|not found>> - ReDoS <worst shape, ratio, ms at the 5 MB limit> - legitimate values <n changed; real route altered n> - counts <5005/305 -> 5044/306 y/n; Build verify line> - CI <n completed success of n; pending <names|none>; failing <names|none>> - CodeQL <analyses n of 3 at the head; Analyze runs complete y/n; open alerts on PR ref n; new high+ n; new error n; #83 #84 #43 instances n; #136 on the PR ref <open|absent>; check-run conclusion <x>> - merge <ahead 3 behind 0 y/n; merge-tree clean y/n and equals GitHub's tree y/n; main sha7 at start and end> - jest <new file 39 y/n; readers n files green> - gitleaks rc <n>)`. Then the sections: Step 0 (sha256s, slot count), REFUSE counts, PINS (start and verdict), instrument and load, Checks 1-8 each with the FAIL clock and the evidence path, the red/green tables, the mutant matrix (mutant, line, prediction, result, killers), the bypass-hunt table (input, mode, output, validator verdict, class A/B/C, sink), the timing table, the run table, findings `B647-n` (severity, `path:line` at the head, instrument, FAIL met, fix-shape in prose, evidence class MEASURED AT RUNTIME / PROBED / READ ONLY; "none" is valid), the builder-claims table (claim, your number, agree y/n), FOR TUESDAY (the verdict in plain words; whether a forward merge is needed (expected no); what stands between the PR and a landing, naming the Analyze runs and `build` if pending; what to read after the landing: alerts #83, #84, #43 BY NUMBER on main's push analysis (any still open is a STOP with the run id) and #136, and the `Deploy demo` run expected `skipped`; the head-pinned MERGE-commit landing, never squash, never rebase; the (C) follow-ups for the product owner), FOUND / TESTED / HOW / NOT TESTED / corrections / processes, ports and trees left, **UNMEASURED**. **Last line, exactly one of:** `VERDICT: B647 pr112 b642/nexusai-validators-777-776 @ <sha7> <GO|GO WITH FINDINGS|NO GO> (round 1 of 2) on main <sha7>` (main by `ls-remote` at verdict; the line carries none of the words that name a landing; the findings ids with severities and the CI state sit on the line above it, e.g. `B647-1 Minor, B647-2 Note; CI pending: build`), or `STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY <one question>`.

**LANDING HOLD (Tuesday's, restated by you in FOR TUESDAY in your own words, done by you never).** After a GO or GO WITH FINDINGS with every check-run complete at the head: Tuesday lands the SAME commit by a MERGE COMMIT, head-pinned: `gh pr merge 112 -R datasecau/Reporting_Dashboard_Au --merge --match-head-commit 412c784bed9792221b87cb8f429941ec6acd15db` under the NexusAI `GH_CONFIG_DIR`. Never squash (C-190/C-68), never rebase, no forward merge, CodeQL never bypassed, no alert dismissed, the ruleset never touched. Then Tuesday closes #67 with a pointer to #112 (the branch `rd-777-776-validators-s92r` stays). The landing starts a `Deploy demo` run (`deploy-demo.yml` on `push` to main): expected every job `skipped` while `CI_DEPLOY_ENABLED` is unset (this gate deploys nothing and reads no variable); anything else, Tuesday stops and reads what ran. After the landing, in a SEPARATE step: read main's push `Build` and the CodeQL push analysis, and alerts #83, #84 and #43 BY NUMBER on `refs/heads/main` (each must read fixed; any still open is a STOP with the run id, never a dismissal) and #136 (not in the aim); the records seat moves RD-777 and RD-776 (both Testing; Jira transition id 31 lands on `Testing`, id 51 lands on `Declined`, the trap) with evidence. This gate does none of it.

**STATUS-NOW (binding).** **Write the STATUS file at Step 0 and keep it updated after every check and every jest hold; a STATUS that does not exist while your logs move is a failure of this brief.** At Step 0, before any heavy work, write `/Volumes/Laptop-DEV/!CODING/Datasec/NexusAI/1_Project_Definition/Briefs/2026-10-25_B647_STATUS.md` holding: the placeholder FIRST line `GATE VERDICT B647: PENDING`; Step 0 (sha256s of source and copy, the slot count with its control, the `brief_seat: model=...` line); the REFUSE counts; PINS (head, merge ref, base, main, `compare` ahead/behind, the open-PR list, the check-run table and the Analyze statuses, the analyses count, at your start); target and hard-stop times written absolute; and one line per check (1-8) saying done / running / not started with the evidence path. **Do NOT write a `VERDICT:`, `STOPPED:` or `READY` line at the start of any line in the file until you mean it (not even as a draft or a quotation): Tuesday's watcher reads only the file's last line.** The LAST LINE while you work is `WORKING: <check and what is running, with a figure that moves>`. Evidence goes in `Briefs/2026-10-25_B647_evidence/` (summaries, hashes, TSVs, mutant diffs, test-output excerpts; no secrets, no Jira token). **Heartbeat:** every waiter and every long job prints a figure that MOVES (a load1 reading, a loop counter `i of N`, elapsed seconds, a growing log size) at least every 30 s into `session-tools/b647/logs/heartbeat.txt`; a figure that does not move for 3 beats means the waiter is stuck: say so in STATUS and what you did. Never wait with `pgrep -f <pattern>` from a shell whose own argv holds the pattern: wait on a recorded pid (`kill -0`) or a done-marker file your job writes last. **RESUME at about 80 percent of your context:** write `WORKING: RESUME NEEDED at Check <n>` and a RESUME section and stop adding work; Tuesday restarts you from that file. A verdict from a gate that did not finish Checks 2, 3a, 3b and 5 is conditional 